{
  "$schema": "../scene.schema.json",
  "id": "briar-glen-river",
  "name": "Briar Glen Quay and the Millweir",
  "description": "Bead mw-e25.11, mw-e25.12, mw-e25.24: the river below Briar Glen as one walkable grey-box scene, about 220 x 60 m. From under the Miners' Bridge (path-up leads back, arrive-from-under-the-bridge arrives) the lit riverbank path runs east, downriver. Briar Glen Quay (x 30..100, bollards, six glenstone block stacks on timber cradles, a crane, the toll shed with its notice) fronts the quay basin, standing water you can swim, freeze into walkable ice or climb out of by two ladders; Mags Oakum's stone barge Patient Ann lies moored against the quay (static placeholder hull and barge-berth, the barge ride is mw-e25.15). Further east the Millweir: a sill and the mill pond (standing water, drained by the sluice wheel into a low state that exposes a stepping-stone path across), a tall weir wall and the sluice walk, a catwalk hung on the downstream face with a 2.4 m gap mid-walk (jump, plank, Blink or rope anchor; a fall drops into the lower pool and never hurts, ladders lead out). The far end of the walk and the pond's far landing are the Briarwood far bank: reaching it by any route writes world.millweir.sluice-walk-open (graph millweir-walk), and the doorway in the far bank's south wall (far-bank-gate) leads on into the Briarwood (arrive-from-briarwood arrives). The towpath goes on east to a wall and the sign for Kestrel Lock: arrive-from-kestrel-lock and the towpath-exit stub (planned mw-e25.14, no transition yet). The Stone Stair slide from the Deepworks' cutting hall arrives at arrive-from-deepworks. Reach it with ?scene=briar-glen-river.",
